WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.637
-Welcome back, everybody!
We are hanging out with BTS!

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.972
Yeah, come on!

00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:10.810
[ Audience screaming ]

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.580
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.616
Being in the biggest band
in the world

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.517
means there's lot of
information out there

00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:19.752
about you on the internet,

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:22.087
but not all of it is true.

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:25.024
I'm going to read a few
BTS rumors I came across,

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:27.660
and you guys tell me
if they are true or not,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.396
and what the story is
behind it, okay?

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:31.864
Does that sound okay?
Will you do it?

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:34.267
-Okay!
-Let's go!

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.602
Let's go!

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.002
-Here we go.

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:40.640
First, is it true that instead
of calling your fans Army,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.009
you were originally
going to call them

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.511
"Bell?"

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.711
-That's true.
-Yes.

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:47.413
So it's kind of true,

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.415
'cause, you know,
when you say BTS,

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:53.086
it stands for
"Bangtan" in Korea,

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.053
not "behind the scene."

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:56.088
I mean, for your information.

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:58.391
It stands for "bangtan,"

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.393
and when you say
"bell" in Korean,

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.628
it sounds like "bang-wool,"

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:05.765
so it starts with
the same word, "bang."

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:09.368
So when we think of
the fan name,

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:12.037
somebody brings up
the idea, like,

00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:13.439
what about the bell thing?

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:15.875
It was like, kind of like --
-Hi, bell!

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:19.245
-Everybody brings their bells
and like, "make some noise!"

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.313
And their bells, like
ring-a-ling-a-ling.

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:22.882
[ Imitating bells ]

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:28.521
But thank God that it has not.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.156
Army's so much better, yeah.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.458
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.794
Can you imagine, everyone
bringing bells to the concerts?

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.962
Ding-a-ling-a-ling-a-ling!

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:38.631
-Kind of cute, though.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.033
-Yeah, it is cute.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:44.337
Makes for a good Christmas song.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:47.340
Jimin, when you guys
were deciding on stage names,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.476
is it true that you
almost decided to go with

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.877
"Baby J?"

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:52.912
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.147
-What else was in the running?

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.031
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.232
-Well, if you decide
to make it longer,

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.800
you can go with Jimin Fallon.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.403
Jimin Fallon.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:24.110
-Thank you, that's perfect.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.012
That's the goal
of this whole thing.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:29.815
All these years,
that's the goal.

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:31.450
-Hi, I'm Jimin Fallon!

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.652
-We're like brothers.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.320
-Yeah.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.555
-Why not? Why not?

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.223
-Alright, V.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:40.192
V, is it is true
that you never actually

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:42.028
intended on auditioning
for BTS,

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.730
you just went to the audition
to support your friend?

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.032
-Swag.
-True.

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:48.935
Yes.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.537
-What happened to your friend?

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.308
[ Laughing ]

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:58.077
-Only me.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.311
-Only V!

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:00.412
-Only V!

00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:01.947
-Okay, victory. Yeah.

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:03.282
-Yeah, oh, victory.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:06.319
-Jin, is it true that you're the
best chef of the group?

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:08.454
What is your speciality dish?

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.123
-It's not fact.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:25.371
[ Applause ]

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.773
-Ohh.

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:29.575
-That's what I'm talking about.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:33.413
Kimchi's my jam. I love it.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.014
I love it, love it, love it.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.315
Here we go.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:40.553
Suga, is it true
that the first album you bought

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.655
was an Eminem CD?

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.756
-Oh.
-Ooh.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.525
-And what did your parents
think of it?

00:04:10.515 --> 00:04:13.852
[ Audience laughing ]

00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:16.589
-J-Hope, I haven't
heard enough from you.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.724
Haven't heard enough
from J-Hope.

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:21.594
Is it true that
you consider yourself

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.530
the most fashionable member
of BTS?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.898
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.100
-Listen to that!
Listen to the crowd!

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.136
-[ Imitating air horns ]
-Listen to the audience!

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.838
Let them speak for you!

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:34.340
That's what I'm talking about.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.474
-Ohhh.

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.843
Absolutely! Yeah!

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:39.111
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:42.481
Yeah, I'm wearing
nice clothing

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:44.450
and short pants

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:48.287
and a slipper with socks, yeah.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.389
[ Laughing ]

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:52.492
-Enough said. Enough said.

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.326
-Okay, okay.

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:56.895
-Finally, you guys have
been together for 8 years.

00:04:56.895 --> 00:04:58.697
What's the most surprising
thing you've learned

00:04:58.697 --> 00:05:00.566
about each other in that time?

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.502
-Oh, V sleeps
with his eyes open.

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.271
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:07.640
-Ohh.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:08.708
-Yeah.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.343
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:15.715
-That's it?
-Yeah!

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.449
-I'm glad we
cleared all that up.

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:18.584
Thank you for doing that.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.086
BTS, everybody!

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:24.223
Their CD single, "Butter,"
is out now.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:27.660
Stick around, because later
BTS will be performing

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.796
their new song,
"Permission to Dance."

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:33.900
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

